{:edb/db-before-t 2568 :edb/db-after-t 2569 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535881 50 #inst "2026-10-09T09:46:19.754Z" 13194139535881 true] [17592186128862 1100 "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535881 false] [17592186128862 1100 "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/34184a95be2b3ae6865fde109ace7e8b4397f4b01982928be73cff4199792d61.png)" 13194139535881 true] [17592186128862 1145 "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The first matrix is not in row echelon form since $a_{32} \\neq 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The fourth matrix is not in row echelon form since, for example, the leading entry $a_{22}$ lies to the left of the leading entry $a_{13}$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535881 false] [17592186128862 1145 "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The first matrix is not in row echelon form since $a_{32} \\neq 0$ (condition II is violated).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/b9f56d3f0414f4b56b50e59c2c02d9072f1fb74ce09d801a1ab62abac61ad737.png)\n\n- The second matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/8562a693df46625ee0dc2bcdecc664dfc50a99889fdb855ae2e06dc1db02a3d4.png)\n\n- The third matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/d263bfe2386309c55f1d63d97d15eaa682e9b0748a9bee6d3378d0b9035927ba.png)\n\n- The fourth matrix is not in row echelon form since, for example, the leading entry $a_{22}$ lies to the left of the leading entry $a_{13}$ (condition II is violated).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/6ccb00b5e1387cd15847c50d66b26ee903d95428bcff2bfc933b675f9b590717.png)" 13194139535881 true] [17592186128863 1100 "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/e300a9ac18f0170ae9053c9635fe13a9dd6def793ebfc0bd9dbe81e28810a347.png)" 13194139535881 true] [17592186128863 1100 "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535881 false] [17592186128863 1145 "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 7 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535881 false] [17592186128863 1145 "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/f3d533c5687da1a75a07c6ad86b40ee8aa6ea5c86cdd250d5c47ff99b885ef61.png)\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/5d576fca72f6a4f9f0668ff0efbdc2cacc33f8dbb2c00192a7397da9ec83adea.png)\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/4f6a034def35760ae94b6eb6a425c59950556a78c124aa9ad0fcfdaa06053b28.png)" 13194139535881 true] [17592186128864 1100 "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535881 false] [17592186128864 1100 "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/085cb01a2e4da286ea19a6f1e1707e685646af3d887abb1a57ab50e4d352c53f.png)" 13194139535881 true] [17592186128864 1145 "Notice that by replacing $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535881 false] [17592186128864 1145 "Notice that by replacing $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/d7b93aa8abed895e49b965b8d0905088249475cad98757e7a93a174fae143b49.png)" 13194139535881 true] [17592186128930 1100 "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535881 false] [17592186128930 1100 "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/a29e80b35c9505ee665a109978de9b936ee7ce59eef631d7af9a4b7954bd8696.png)" 13194139535881 true] [17592186128930 1145 "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071571/assets/d2f89fe83787daf667e01fd4c4fe644bc36cfe23b046088c22e8de17bb02dc28.png)\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$" 13194139535881 true] [17592186128930 1145 "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$" 13194139535881 false] [17592186129048 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372217 13194139535881 true] [17592186129048 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372245 13194139535881 true] [17592186129048 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372252 13194139535881 true] [17592186129049 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372196 13194139535881 true] [17592186129049 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372203 13194139535881 true] [17592186129049 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372210 13194139535881 true] [17592186129049 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372231 13194139535881 true] [17592186129049 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372238 13194139535881 true] [17592186129050 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372224 13194139535881 true] [17592186129050 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372280 13194139535881 true] [17592186129111 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372189 13194139535881 true] [17592186129111 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372259 13194139535881 true] [17592186129111 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372266 13194139535881 true] [17592186129111 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372273 13194139535881 true] [17592186129708 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535881 true] [17592186129708 1100 "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535881 true] [17592186129708 1100 "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535881 false] [17592186129708 1145 "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form." 13194139535881 true] [17592186372189 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372190 13194139535881 true] [17592186372189 1089 "q-129210" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372189 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535881 true] [17592186372189 1100 "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $2$nd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372189 1113 #uuid "ea048481-9a85-5459-a314-8e26e851ea3b" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372189 1145 "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $2$nd and $4$th rows of  $A$ are $1$ and $3$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $1+3=4.$" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372190 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372191 13194139535881 true] [17592186372190 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372192 13194139535881 true] [17592186372190 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372193 13194139535881 true] [17592186372190 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372194 13194139535881 true] [17592186372190 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372195 13194139535881 true] [17592186372190 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535881 true] [17592186372190 1041 "selection" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372190 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372194 13194139535881 true] [17592186372190 1110 #uuid "e318616d-791c-5a03-93a3-ac99c3733229" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372191 1034 "-8" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372191 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535881 true] [17592186372191 1111 #uuid "d9a2383a-c510-51c6-9e69-2b4ee557a3f1" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372192 1034 "8" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372192 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535881 true] [17592186372192 1111 #uuid "740e1620-f50b-587e-8103-ddc3553daa71" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372193 1034 "2" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372193 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535881 true] [17592186372193 1111 #uuid "4d68997f-19cd-5561-b23e-ed63bb45b2c6" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372194 1034 "4" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372194 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535881 true] [17592186372194 1111 #uuid "33f5c5e9-20d6-55ef-8096-86e9af3e487e" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372195 1034 "-6" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372195 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535881 true] [17592186372195 1111 #uuid "72c41345-bcc1-5a94-bc43-17008d0a509b" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372196 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372197 13194139535881 true] [17592186372196 1089 "q-129213" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372196 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535881 true] [17592186372196 1100 "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372196 1113 #uuid "6061d8ea-d309-5b82-8a65-c5a4fc1b804c" 13194139535881 true] [17592186372196 1145 "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form." 13194139535881 true] [17592186372197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372198 13194139535881 true] [17592186372197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372199 13194139535881 true] [17592186372197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372200 13194139535881 true] [17592186372197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372201 13194139535881 true] [17592186372197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372202 13194139535881 true] [17